# Code owners for Proxima.
#
# GitHub applies these rules top to bottom and **the last matching pattern
# wins** — it does not union the matches. So the global rule goes first and the
# specific areas go below it; anything you add later must be more specific than
# the line above it or it will silently take over.
#
# Teams live in the `proxima-search` organisation.

# Global fallback: anything not claimed below.
*                           @proxima-search/maintainers

# Vector space, distance kernels, slot allocator, top-k, metadata. Changing a
# kernel changes every number in BENCHMARKS.md, so this area is reviewed by the
# people who own those numbers.
/crates/proxima-core/       @proxima-search/core

# VectorIndex, FlatIndex, HnswIndex, IvfPqIndex, recall_at_k. Recall is a
# correctness property here, not a nice-to-have.
/crates/proxima-index/      @proxima-search/index

# WAL, snapshots, Collection. Durability bugs are the ones you find in
# production at 3am; this area gets a durability reviewer.
/crates/proxima-store/      @proxima-search/storage

# Hand-written HTTP and JSON, the public API surface, metrics.
/crates/proxima-server/     @proxima-search/server

# CI, release automation, and anything that can run with a token.
/.github/                   @proxima-search/maintainers @proxima-search/release

# Prose. Reviewed for the "every number is a measured number" rule.
/docs/                      @proxima-search/docs @proxima-search/maintainers
